+- basis: run 01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X, workflow version c25ec2416a5e45108d80b6ea43ca9f9e394a3f8fab9ed6d0e53cfa2d3e45bdfa, commit 592f64bd92615069d6a7dbf32cc98c75eabb74e6
+- revised_at_commit: 592f64bd92615069d6a7dbf32cc98c75eabb74e6 (ADR-0015: engine drift signal for later judgement)
+
+## Findings
+
+### Qualitygate: add a loop-asset tier with a checked-in evidence-smoke.nu regression — filed fabro-bfe1
+The qualitygate deterministically verified nothing for loop-asset changes (evidence.nu, reviewer.md): 4.15s run, "no crates touched". Fix: a loop-asset tier in the qualitygate recipe plus a checked-in mixed-capture scratch exercise `evidence-smoke.nu` following the `closeout-smoke.nu` pattern. Effect: deterministic verification, durable regression, fewer manual LLM-verification turns. Not duplicates of fabro-50f8 / fabro-574d (thematic overlap only, cross-referenced in the seed).
+
+### Engine: re-resolve stage prompt files from the run branch tip — filed fabro-c080
+The reviewer judged under the pre-change prompt snapshot; correct only by luck of an on-disk cross-check. Fix: re-resolve prompt files from the run branch tip at stage start, or inject a "this run modified your prompt" notice; same mechanism fabro-dc81 requests for `[run.pull_request]`. Effect: prompt-editing seeds can never silently review under superseded instructions.
