 {"id":"fabro-55a7","title":"Planner: batch reconnaissance into one shell call (sd ready + sd show + base-branch grep)","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:28:38.909Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:38:45.247Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md, batch reconnaissance into a single shell call instead of many tool calls. In the basis run the two planner passes spent 92.0 s and 93.5 s inference over 8 separate calls each; the in-flight check alone took 3 round-trips. Expected ~40-60 s and ~$0.06 saved per pass (36% of run cost was planner), and a shorter claim-to-dispatch window (21 s here) narrows the duplicate-claim race. Basis: run 01M23RQRCB748R4VRXA2WE6BZ0, workflow version 3b17faf145735aa14caf619a38c0b079a1ff1c91acf24211c9ab08a2612c6f6f, commit d55d6ea53c41f53c116ba063221f2988223072dd","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-9d2f","title":"Engine: a steered/failed stage's abandoned worktree diff must not be committed by later cycles — quarantine residue between cycles","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:24:04.137Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:38:36.777Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"INCIDENT 2026-09-09 (run 01M23RQRCB748R4VRXA2WE6BZ0, PR #109): the duplicate-6a5a cycle was steered to fail at implementer (19:14:37Z); the implementer correctly 'abandoned in place, not committed' its diff (auto_merge=false in 3 workflow.tomls + pull_request.rs logging). The Blocked route returned to the planner, which claimed a DIFFERENT seed (fabro-e702); the next cycle ran on the SAME worktree and its deterministic closeout committed EVERYTHING — the abandoned residue rode into PR #109 alongside e702's legitimate prompt work and was approved by a reviewer who saw loop files as counts-only. Line-watch closed #109 unmerged (auto-merge would have landed the residue and re-contradicted the recorded user auto-merge decision fabro-d114). Wanted: when a stage fails (or is steered to abort), the engine quarantines/resets the uncommitted worktree state before the next cycle starts — or the closeout's diff assembly only includes files touched since the CURRENT seed's claim, with residue surfaced as a blocking anomaly. Also worth covering: one-seed-per-run discipline after a mid-run failure (the planner re-planned a second seed in the same run — the loop Bound expected by the planner prompt). Acceptance: engine test proving a failed stage's residue cannot reach a later cycle's commit/PR; closeout diff scoping test; clippy/fmt clean. Basis: run 01M23RQRCB748R4VRXA2WE6BZ0 journal + events (stage.failed 19:14:47Z, cycle-2 claim fabro-e702), PR #109 diff, line-watch close 2026-09-09 ~19:30Z. REVISOR CORROBORATION (run 01M23SSXSB1, PR #110): independent revisor finding fabro-e19f proposed the same class ('roll back or side-ref the worktree diff when a stage fails deterministically') — folded here; e19f closed as duplicate.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
 {"id":"fabro-c0e5","title":"Evidence capture must flag out-of-spec seed-work files (residue detection), not just demote loop files to counts-only","status":"open","type":"bug","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:24:04.235Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:38:36.961Z","assignee":"fabro","description":"Same incident as the residue seed (run 01M23RQRCB748R4VRXA2WE6BZ0, PR #109): the evidence capture classified .fabro/workflows/*/workflow.toml changes as loop churn (counts-only), so the reviewer NEVER SAW that the PR's core semantic content (auto_merge=false across three workflows) was out-of-spec residue from a steered-failed cycle — and approved. The known classifier painpoint (promote loop files when the SPEC names them, journaled in run 01M230P8RGN) covers expected loop-work; this is the inverse case: loop/seed-work files changed that the spec does NOT name must surface as a named, diffed ANOMALY section, not disappear into counts. Wanted: the evidence capture (and/or the reviewer prompt) treats any changed file outside the claimed seed's spec scope as a first-class finding: full diff + 'not named by the seed spec' marker; the reviewer must adjudicate it explicitly (residue vs adjacent repair vs scope creep). Acceptance: evidence.nu/reviewer test with an out-of-spec workflow.toml change proving it appears named+diffed, not counts-only. Basis: PR #109 evidence + review (approved with invisible auto_merge flip), run 01M230P8RGN journal (the classifier painpoint), PR #109 close evidence. REVISOR CORROBORATION (PR #110, fabro-d898 folded): the reviewer-side mirror — account for EVERY file in the run-base diff, including sub-claim-base changes the current seed did not touch — belongs to this seed's anomaly-section design; d898 closed as duplicate.","labels":["engine","workflows"]}
