+{"id":"fabro-bfe1","title":"Qualitygate: add a loop-asset tier with a checked-in evidence-smoke.nu regression","status":"open","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-09T19:47:40.355Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:47:40.355Z","description":"Run 01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X: the tester's 'just qualitygate' ran 4.15s with 'no crates touched / format clean' — zero machine verification of the actual changes (evidence.nu, reviewer.md). Verification fell to the two costliest LLM stages: implementer hand-built a scratch-git exercise (216s inference) and the reviewer re-ran it (57s), then the regression exercise was deleted at closeout. Change: in the qualitygate recipe (justfile / scripts/qualitygate.nu) add a loop-asset tier — a 'nu -c source' check for .fabro/workflows/develop/scripts/*.nu plus a checked-in mixed-capture scratch exercise as evidence-smoke.nu following the existing closeout-smoke.nu pattern. Effect: deterministic verification of loop-asset changes, durable regression coverage, fewer manual-verification turns. Distinct from fabro-50f8 (prompt-mandated ad-hoc exercises) and fabro-574d (crate derivation): gate infrastructure plus a durable checked-in regression. Basis: run 01M23TE61D4Y33415BK5M7C70X, workflow version c25ec2416a5e45108d80b6ea43ca9f9e394a3f8fab9ed6d0e53cfa2d3e45bdfa, commit 592f64bd92615069d6a7dbf32cc98c75eabb74e6","labels":["revision"]}
